WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.403
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:04.738
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:07.173
between Coca-Cola in the UK and the US.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.641
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.982
In the UK, regular Coke
comes in eight portion sizes,

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:18.785
starting with this mini can,
which is 150 milliliters.

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.553
Then we have three
options which all include

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:22.422
250 milliliters of Coke.

00:00:22.422 --> 00:00:24.991
Then we have our standard
can, which is 330 milliliters.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.894
Our standard plastic
bottle is 500 milliliters.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:30.163
From there, we move up to
this bottle, which is 1 liter.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:31.931
1.25 liters,

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.533
1.5 liters,

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.035
and 2.25 liters.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:36.536
It's worth noting that
these ones are only stocked

00:00:36.536 --> 00:00:39.072
by a limited number of
shops, including Iceland.

00:00:39.072 --> 00:00:40.640
The supermarket chain, not the country.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.910
And in the US, our classic
Coke comes in these sizes.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.446
The mini can, which is 7.5 ounces.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:48.982
Then this mini bottle, which is 8 ounces.

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:51.151
Then we jump up to the
standard 12-ounce can.

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:53.319
That also comes in a
little 12-ounce bottle.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:56.890
From there, we got this guy,
which is the 16.9 fluid ounces,

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.259
aka 500 milliliters.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.327
Then we have a 20-ounce bottle.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:03.096
And finally, our biggest, the 2 liter,

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.734
which is also 67.6 ounces.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.737
Now, that means as far as
Coca-Cola classic is concerned,

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:14.674
the UK's largest size
is actually 12.5% larger

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:15.675
than that in the US.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.677
There is a reason why we're
specifying regular Coke here.

00:01:17.677 --> 00:01:19.579
The UK government brought in a sugar tax,

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.081
which raised the price of sugary drinks

00:01:21.081 --> 00:01:23.049
in an effort to reduce
people's sugar consumption.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:25.085
Instead of raising the prices
of some of their drinks,

00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:26.486
what Coca-Cola did was just to make

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.621
the sugary versions of their
drinks a little bit smaller.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:30.924
For example, how the normal
largest size of regular Coke

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.859
is 1.5 liters,

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:35.662
whereas the largest size
of Coke Zero is 2 liters.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:38.364
Whereas here in the US, we
don't have a specific sugar tax.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.834
So we can get our bottles of
classic Coke and diet Coke

00:01:40.834 --> 00:01:42.535
in the same size and for the same price.

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.404
As a consequence of the UK sugar rules,

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:46.873
it actually means that
the 2.25 regular Coke

00:01:46.873 --> 00:01:48.641
isn't our largest bottle size.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:49.709
That crown

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:50.610
[thud]

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.744
goes to this,

00:01:51.744 --> 00:01:53.713
the 3-liter diet Coke bottle.

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:56.015
Now, this absolute unit is 50% larger

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:57.750
than the biggest bottle in America.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.619
If you're doing, like, a party, maybe?

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:00.920
If you're buying that for yourself,

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:03.089
like, you've got a problem.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:03.923
I'm sorry.

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:07.460
That is ridiculously huge
and really hilarious.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.597
Now, I want to point
out that on Walmart.com,

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:15.602
they have this 3-liter
bottle of diet Coke on it,

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.570
but it's not available anywhere.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.773
So my assumption is at one
point in the United States,

00:02:20.773 --> 00:02:22.909
there was 3-liter bottles available.

00:02:22.909 --> 00:02:24.210
But if Walmart doesn't have it,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.612
I'm assuming it isn't anywhere.

00:02:25.612 --> 00:02:27.647
That being said, in terms
of multipack options,

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:29.082
the US still comes out on top.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.718
Our single largest multipack

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:35.355
is the 35-pack of 12-ounce cans.

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:37.357
Let's get a picture of that on the screen.

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:39.792
I ordered it online, and
here's what they sent me.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:47.133
24-pack, and nine loose cans.

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.502
Now, correct me if I'm wrong,
but what's 24 plus nine?

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:50.637
It ain't 35.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:52.772
And when I emailed the
place that I bought it from,

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.108
they said, "Oh, sorry,
you're missing two cans,

00:02:55.108 --> 00:02:56.376
so we'll just refund you the two cans."

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.411
And I'm like, "No, I
don't want the two cans,

00:02:58.411 --> 00:02:59.879
I want the 35-pack

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:01.781
'cause that's what I'm
doing for this video,"

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:03.883
and they just sent me $2
back, so thank you for that.

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:06.853
Anyway, so then I go, nuts to this.

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:08.655
I'm going to Walmart.com.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:10.557
Give me the 35-pack.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.591
Buy. Enter.

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.526
And then they sent me

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:20.667
three 12-packs, which
is more than 35 cans,

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.101
so I guess technically
they're being generous,

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:25.205
but once again, it's not
that I need 35 cans of soda.

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:28.374
I need the 35-can pack for
this video specifically.

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:31.811
There's a 35-can pack
somewhere in America,

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:35.515
and everyone's just sending
me roughly 35 cans of soda.

00:03:35.515 --> 00:03:36.482
Thank you for that.

00:03:36.482 --> 00:03:38.551
Our largest single item is this.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:45.258
This is a 24-pack of 330-milliliter cans,

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:47.894
which comes to a total of 7.92 liters.

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:52.699
Here is everything that's in regular Coke.

00:03:52.699 --> 00:03:53.733
Harry: Carbonated water.
Joe: Carbonated water.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.667
Harry: Sugar.
Joe: High-fructose corn syrup.

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.236
Harry: Color (caramel E150d).
Joe: Caramel color.

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:57.237
Harry: Phosphoric acid.
Joe: Phosphoric acid.

00:03:57.237 --> 00:03:58.805
Harry: And natural flavorings,
Joe: And natural flavors.

00:03:58.805 --> 00:03:59.872
Harry: including caffeine.
Joe: Caffeine.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.641
Now, obviously we don't get
a full ingredients list,

00:04:01.641 --> 00:04:04.244
because the recipe of Coca-Cola
is a closely guarded secret.

00:04:04.244 --> 00:04:05.778
At the World of Coca-Cola in Atlanta,

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:08.214
there's reportedly a vault which
contains the secret formula

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:09.649
written down on a piece of paper.

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:12.452
Who cares if the recipe gets loose?

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:14.821
Coca-Cola, no one's gonna edge you up.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:16.256
Pepsi can't beat you.

00:04:16.256 --> 00:04:17.123
Who cares?

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.591
I mean, how do you even make cola?

00:04:18.591 --> 00:04:19.792
You probably just go into the factory

00:04:19.792 --> 00:04:21.394
and eyeball it and figure it out.

00:04:21.394 --> 00:04:23.763
It's not super famous because
you don't know how to make it,

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:26.699
it's super famous because
they edged everybody out.

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:27.900
You won.

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:28.735
Do you – I don't care.

00:04:28.735 --> 00:04:29.602
Do you want the recipe?

00:04:29.602 --> 00:04:30.270
I couldn't care less.

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.005
So, what do we know about the recipe?

00:04:32.005 --> 00:04:33.172
Well, there is one obvious difference,

00:04:33.172 --> 00:04:35.942
and that's the use of
high-fructose corn syrup in the US

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.844
versus the use of sugar in the UK.

00:04:38.011 --> 00:04:40.246
Corn syrup is everywhere in American food.

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.315
It's cheaper for manufacturers to use

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:44.484
because the government gives
subsidies to corn farmers,

00:04:44.484 --> 00:04:47.186
keeping the corn supply
high and the prices low.

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.521
Should you be worried about consuming

00:04:48.521 --> 00:04:49.722
high-fructose corn syrup?

00:04:49.722 --> 00:04:51.157
The short answer is not really.

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:52.358
Some studies have suggested

00:04:52.358 --> 00:04:53.459
that the negative effects of sugar

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.795
tend to come from fructose
rather than from glucose,

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.730
but the high fructose in
high-fructose corn syrup

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.232
only relates to its fructose content

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.900
in relation to other corn syrups.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.235
It actually still has less fructose

00:05:02.235 --> 00:05:03.836
than table sugar or than honey.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.372
The main difference it
causes might be the taste.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.408
You've heard Americans
talk about Mexican Coke.

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:10.143
You can find it in most
Mexican restaurants

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:11.277
and in some grocery stores

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:13.513
next to the regular Coke
in the glass bottle.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:15.281
Mexican Coke is made with cane sugar;

00:05:15.281 --> 00:05:17.650
our regular Coke is made with
high-fructose corn syrup.

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:20.153
People tend to like the Mexican Coke more

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:21.988
because it has a sweeter sugary taste.

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:26.092
So right now to compare and contrast,

00:05:26.092 --> 00:05:27.727
I'm going to do a blind taste test

00:05:27.727 --> 00:05:31.731
of both American Coke and Mexican Coke.

00:05:31.731 --> 00:05:32.899
Hang on.

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:36.269
And Harry was nice enough to send me

00:05:36.269 --> 00:05:38.338
a United Kingdom Coke.

00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:40.673
I've also got some British
Coke, some Mexican Coke,

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:41.841
and some American Coke.

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:42.942
I'm now going to blindfold myself

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.377
and let our camera operator, Sarah,

00:05:44.377 --> 00:05:46.312
pour the Cokes out for me.

00:05:46.312 --> 00:05:47.980
I'm blindfolded. I don't
know which one's which.

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.082
I'm going to try them one after the other

00:05:49.082 --> 00:05:50.316
and try and figure out which one's which.

00:05:50.316 --> 00:05:52.051
I'm going to start on the right.

00:05:53.252 --> 00:05:55.021
Hm. See, it could just be mind games,

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:57.623
but that doesn't taste like
exactly what I'm used to.

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:58.725
No. 2.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.628
Ooh. OK. That one tastes pretty good.

00:06:02.628 --> 00:06:03.763
No. 3.

00:06:03.763 --> 00:06:05.732
These two taste pretty similar.

00:06:06.666 --> 00:06:08.301
This one tastes a bit
weird for some reason.

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:12.372
I'm going to guess that this
one is American, on the right.

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:14.841
I was expecting more of a
difference, I'll be honest.

00:06:14.841 --> 00:06:18.211
I'll go with British in the
middle, Mexican on my left.

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:20.246
Put them in front of me, and
then I'll unblindfold myself.

00:06:21.848 --> 00:06:22.849
Wow. OK.

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:24.650
That was Mexican Coke.

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.953
I was right about British.

00:06:26.953 --> 00:06:29.355
I just got Mexican and
American Coke mixed up.

00:06:29.355 --> 00:06:30.189
Wow. OK.

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:32.625
A lot of people have really
hyped up Mexican Coke to me,

00:06:32.625 --> 00:06:34.594
and I honestly, like,

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:36.229
that was my least favorite of the three.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:45.505
They taste exactly the same.

00:06:45.505 --> 00:06:50.042
So I'm going to go UK, Mexico, USA.

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:50.977
Wow, really?

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:53.713
["America the Beautiful" plays]

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:57.150
I'm so great at pointless things!

00:06:57.283 --> 00:06:58.951
Any other ingredients to look out for?

00:06:58.951 --> 00:07:00.586
Well, one of them might be caramel color.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:02.388
As we know, certain
classes of caramel color

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:04.857
have a byproduct which has
been linked to causing cancer.

00:07:04.857 --> 00:07:06.859
Unfortunately, the caramel E150d

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:09.362
that Coke in the UK uses
is one of these classes.

00:07:09.362 --> 00:07:11.297
We reached out to Coca-Cola here in the US

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:12.565
to see if that was the case,

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:15.134
because the type is not
specified on the label.

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:16.869
They told us that it is in fact

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:21.040
the same E150d caramel
color in the States.

00:07:21.274 --> 00:07:22.475
But what about diet Coke?

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:23.910
It still contains caramel color,

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:26.245
but instead of using sugar
and corn syrup to sweeten it,

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:28.181
in the US it's sweetened with aspartame,

00:07:28.181 --> 00:07:29.982
and in the UK it's
sweetened with aspartame

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:31.617
as well acesulfame K.

00:07:31.617 --> 00:07:33.953
The good news is that both
the EU and the FDA say

00:07:33.953 --> 00:07:36.088
that acesulfame K is safe for consumption.

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:37.623
In terms of the difference with Coke Zero,

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:41.360
in the US, our Coke Zero uses
ace K as well as aspartame.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.795
Rumors have existed for years claiming

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:44.297
that aspartame causes cancer,

00:07:44.297 --> 00:07:46.599
but it turns out that that
is likely to be false.

00:07:46.599 --> 00:07:48.901
The claims originated from
some Italian researchers

00:07:48.901 --> 00:07:50.536
way back in 2005.

00:07:50.536 --> 00:07:52.205
I feel like I heard about
that in the '80s, but OK.

00:07:52.205 --> 00:07:53.806
People were quick to call their methods

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:55.842
and results into question.

00:07:55.842 --> 00:07:57.243
The FDA says, "the use of aspartame

00:07:57.243 --> 00:07:58.945
as a general ... sweetener ... is safe."

00:07:58.945 --> 00:08:00.913
While the European Food
Safety Authority says,

00:08:00.913 --> 00:08:02.915
"Studies do not suggest an increased risk

00:08:02.915 --> 00:08:04.617
associated with the aspartame consumption

00:08:04.617 --> 00:08:07.220
for ... leukemia, brain tumours
or a variety of cancers."

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:09.755
There's a cool side effect for Coke

00:08:09.755 --> 00:08:12.024
using these artificial sweeteners
you might not know about.

00:08:12.024 --> 00:08:14.861
Because they're so much more
sweet than sugar per pound,

00:08:14.861 --> 00:08:17.530
there's a tiny amount of them
dissolved in your diet Coke

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.365
compared to the amount of
sugar that's in a classic Coke.

00:08:19.365 --> 00:08:22.401
That means a can of Coke is
denser than that of a diet Coke.

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:24.837
So when you put said Coke in water ...

00:08:26.706 --> 00:08:27.707
to the bottom.

00:08:27.707 --> 00:08:28.708
Diet Coke ...

00:08:32.945 --> 00:08:33.913
floats.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:35.748
One other rumor we felt
compelled to address

00:08:35.748 --> 00:08:37.917
was the role of cocaine in Coca-Cola.

00:08:37.917 --> 00:08:39.418
This dates right back to the 1800s

00:08:39.418 --> 00:08:40.386
when the drink was invented.

00:08:40.386 --> 00:08:42.421
Coca-Cola's official stance on this

00:08:42.421 --> 00:08:45.591
is that there's never been
cocaine in any of its products.

00:08:45.591 --> 00:08:49.529
What it does seem to contain,
however, is coca extract.

00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:52.031
Coca is the plant from
which cocaine is extracted.

00:08:52.031 --> 00:08:53.933
Fluid extract of coca was
one of the ingredients

00:08:53.933 --> 00:08:55.968
in a list "This American Life" discovered

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:57.236
which was reportedly a recipe

00:08:57.236 --> 00:08:58.804
for an early version of Coca-Cola.

00:08:58.804 --> 00:09:00.172
And it seems like they're still using it.

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:03.075
In 1988, a Coca-Cola spokesperson said,

00:09:03.075 --> 00:09:05.177
"Ingredients from the coca leaf are used,

00:09:05.177 --> 00:09:07.246
but there is no cocaine in it

00:09:07.246 --> 00:09:09.148
and it all is being tightly overseen

00:09:09.148 --> 00:09:10.683
by regulatory authorities."

00:09:10.683 --> 00:09:12.952
What's fun is that Coca-Cola
got a specific exemption

00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:15.021
from the United Nations
in order to keep using

00:09:15.021 --> 00:09:16.622
coca extract as an ingredient.

00:09:16.622 --> 00:09:18.357
Specifically, Article 27

00:09:18.357 --> 00:09:21.327
of the Single Convention
on Narcotic Drugs of 1961.

00:09:21.761 --> 00:09:22.795
There's only one facility in the US

00:09:22.795 --> 00:09:24.764
licensed to import and process coca leaves

00:09:24.764 --> 00:09:27.166
through a special deal with the DEA.

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:29.502
It is owned by the Stepan Company,

00:09:29.502 --> 00:09:31.170
and it's in Maywood, New Jersey.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.672
According to the Peruvian officials,

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:36.042
they buy around 100 metric tons

00:09:36.042 --> 00:09:39.345
of dried Peruvian coca leaves each year.

00:09:39.345 --> 00:09:41.714
They reportedly process
them and de-cocanize them,

00:09:41.714 --> 00:09:43.516
taking all of the cocaine out of them.

00:09:43.516 --> 00:09:46.218
The cocaine is sold to hospitals
for use as an anesthetic,

00:09:46.218 --> 00:09:47.687
and the cocaine-free extract

00:09:47.687 --> 00:09:49.555
is then sent to Coca-Cola
for use in their products.

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:52.625
Coca-Cola's official line
on the subject is, quote,

00:09:52.625 --> 00:09:54.827
"Coca-Cola does not contain cocaine

00:09:54.827 --> 00:09:56.862
or any other harmful substance,

00:09:56.862 --> 00:09:58.831
and cocaine has never been

00:09:58.831 --> 00:10:01.000
an added ingredient in Coca-Cola."

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:01.767
End quote.

00:10:01.968 --> 00:10:04.403
But it's fair to say that
cocaine and coca extract

00:10:04.403 --> 00:10:05.571
are not the same thing.

00:10:05.571 --> 00:10:07.106
So the latter might in fact be

00:10:07.106 --> 00:10:08.908
one of their not-so-secret
secret ingredients.

00:10:12.478 --> 00:10:14.246
Here are all the Coca-Cola
products in the UK

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:15.648
that you won't find in the US.

00:10:15.648 --> 00:10:18.117
And here's all the Coca-Cola
items you'll find in the US

00:10:18.117 --> 00:10:19.318
that you cannot find in the UK.

00:10:19.318 --> 00:10:20.820
I want to start with two exclusive flavors

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:22.788
you can get in the US
you can't get in the UK.

00:10:22.788 --> 00:10:23.756
They're these two right here,

00:10:23.756 --> 00:10:25.891
cherry vanilla and orange vanilla.

00:10:26.092 --> 00:10:27.326
Cherry vanilla seems pretty standard.

00:10:27.326 --> 00:10:29.095
I think I've had this a bunch of times.

00:10:29.095 --> 00:10:31.097
It's great. It's refreshing. I enjoy it.

00:10:31.664 --> 00:10:33.165
We can't get cherry vanilla in the UK,

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:35.201
but we can get cherry
and we can get vanilla,

00:10:35.201 --> 00:10:36.402
so I guess I can make my own.

00:10:38.304 --> 00:10:40.006
Oh, God. Ah!

00:10:40.006 --> 00:10:41.741
[exhales]

00:10:43.142 --> 00:10:44.343
[exhales]

00:10:44.343 --> 00:10:45.678
Panic over.

00:10:45.678 --> 00:10:47.613
The smart thing to do would
be to mix these in a glass,

00:10:47.613 --> 00:10:48.848
but I'm not a smart man.

00:10:52.018 --> 00:10:52.852
Ah.

00:10:52.852 --> 00:10:54.420
Pretty good.

00:10:54.420 --> 00:10:56.322
The only exclusive Coke
flavor we can currently get –

00:10:56.322 --> 00:10:57.189
[coughs] sorry.

00:10:57.189 --> 00:10:58.991
The only exclusive Coke
flavor we can currently get

00:10:58.991 --> 00:11:01.460
in the UK is this one, which
is diet Coke Sublime Lime.

00:11:01.694 --> 00:11:02.595
As the name suggests,

00:11:02.595 --> 00:11:04.030
it's just diet Coke flavored with lime.

00:11:04.030 --> 00:11:05.931
Next up, caffeine-free Coca-Cola,

00:11:05.965 --> 00:11:08.901
not to be confused with
caffeine-free diet Coke,

00:11:08.901 --> 00:11:10.970
which is what you guys
have over there in the UK.

00:11:10.970 --> 00:11:13.372
Apparently that's your
only caffeine-free option?

00:11:13.372 --> 00:11:14.273
For shame.

00:11:14.273 --> 00:11:15.608
This one is delicious.

00:11:15.608 --> 00:11:16.909
It actually tastes just like Coke.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:18.511
It's perfect for after 2 p.m.

00:11:18.511 --> 00:11:20.112
when you want to keep
drinking soda, like me.

00:11:20.513 --> 00:11:22.615
But if you like caffeine

00:11:22.615 --> 00:11:24.216
and you want a little bit of a boost,

00:11:24.216 --> 00:11:27.319
Coke Energy I believe is
available in both countries,

00:11:27.319 --> 00:11:29.488
but one exclusive Coke Energy flavor

00:11:29.488 --> 00:11:31.891
you can't get in the UK is this.

00:11:31.891 --> 00:11:34.727
The Coke Energy zero sugar.

00:11:34.727 --> 00:11:37.129
The Coke Energy drinks
are being phased out.

00:11:37.129 --> 00:11:37.963
I can't imagine why.

00:11:37.963 --> 00:11:39.165
I think they're actually really good.

00:11:39.165 --> 00:11:43.035
In fact, I went ahead
and got the other ones.

00:11:43.035 --> 00:11:45.337
Regular. I don't really like zero sugar,

00:11:45.337 --> 00:11:47.406
but I do like just regular.

00:11:52.111 --> 00:11:53.646
Oh, yeah.

00:11:53.646 --> 00:11:55.114
I'm into that.

00:11:55.114 --> 00:11:56.115
Yeah, thank you.

00:11:57.683 --> 00:11:59.151
It's good. I mean, like ...

00:12:01.087 --> 00:12:03.856
energy meter's going up, Yuelei!

00:12:03.856 --> 00:12:05.224
Going up!

00:12:08.360 --> 00:12:11.130
If you're like me and
you love soda and coffee,

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.399
Coke in the US has you covered with these.

00:12:13.566 --> 00:12:18.404
You got caramel, vanilla,
vanilla no sugar,

00:12:18.404 --> 00:12:21.507
dark blend, and dark blend zero sugar.

00:12:21.774 --> 00:12:24.977
Oh, my God, I sincerely
love these so much.

00:12:26.112 --> 00:12:28.314
Zero sugar can go there.

00:12:28.314 --> 00:12:29.615
Ooh, which one do I want?

00:12:33.219 --> 00:12:34.053
Hits the spot.

00:12:34.053 --> 00:12:36.489
The I-want-to-jack-my-caffeine-levels-

00:12:36.489 --> 00:12:38.090
through-the-roof spot.

00:12:38.090 --> 00:12:39.792
Dude, Coke and coffee's good together.

00:12:39.792 --> 00:12:41.327
Has anyone had two of
these at the same time?

00:12:41.327 --> 00:12:42.528
I don't think they have.

00:12:45.731 --> 00:12:46.966
They don't mix very well.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:50.236
But individually they're great.

00:12:51.237 --> 00:12:52.204
Uh-oh.

00:12:57.843 --> 00:12:58.711
I might have overdone it.

00:12:58.711 --> 00:13:00.112
We don't have Coke coffees in the UK.

00:13:00.112 --> 00:13:02.181
However, Coca-Cola owns Costa Coffee,

00:13:02.181 --> 00:13:03.582
which is a coffee chain in the UK,

00:13:03.582 --> 00:13:05.117
and they produce canned coffees.

00:13:05.117 --> 00:13:07.253
So I guess, again, I
can try and make my own.

00:13:08.187 --> 00:13:11.490
So, the issue here is
they do do Americanos,

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:13.025
but I got latte instead.

00:13:14.493 --> 00:13:18.063
So see how well milk
combines with Coke, I guess.

00:13:20.766 --> 00:13:23.869
Yeah. Um. [laughs]

00:13:23.869 --> 00:13:26.572
Regretting quite a lot
of things right now.

00:13:26.572 --> 00:13:29.275
Namely all the life choices
that led me to this point.

00:13:29.275 --> 00:13:30.109
Cheers.

00:13:40.386 --> 00:13:41.587
Nope.

00:13:43.055 --> 00:13:44.290
Not even a little bit.

00:13:44.290 --> 00:13:45.591
No, no, no.

00:13:45.591 --> 00:13:46.458
Don't do that.

00:13:46.458 --> 00:13:47.293
No one else do that.

00:13:47.293 --> 00:13:48.861
Please, God. Ugh.

00:13:48.861 --> 00:13:51.497
Just like really watery, fizzy coffee

00:13:51.497 --> 00:13:54.400
that is kind of sweet and ... ugh.

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:55.434
No. Bad.

00:13:56.335 --> 00:13:58.304
The final exclusive
range in the UK is this,

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.839
Coca-Cola signature mixers.

00:14:00.072 --> 00:14:01.307
Coca-Cola worked with bartenders

00:14:01.307 --> 00:14:03.409
to design special Cokes
with different flavors

00:14:03.409 --> 00:14:04.844
which are designed to
be used in cocktails.

00:14:04.977 --> 00:14:08.514
These come with smoky notes, spicy notes,

00:14:08.514 --> 00:14:10.182
herbal notes, and woody notes.

00:14:10.282 --> 00:14:12.151
Tag yourself. I am spicy notes.

00:14:12.318 --> 00:14:12.985
Cool.

00:14:13.586 --> 00:14:15.654
[rumbling]

00:14:15.654 --> 00:14:18.157
My stomach is making some weird
noises after drinking that.

00:14:18.157 --> 00:14:20.726
No one else do that, please, God. Ugh!

00:14:20.726 --> 00:14:22.094
Apparently these are
designed to be enjoyed

00:14:22.094 --> 00:14:23.629
with premium dark spirits.

00:14:23.629 --> 00:14:25.631
Now, I know nothing about
mixology, but thankfully,

00:14:25.631 --> 00:14:27.433
a bartender friend from Australia

00:14:27.433 --> 00:14:28.500
came through with a recipe.

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:30.669
So now I'm going to use
the smoky notes Coca-Cola

00:14:30.669 --> 00:14:31.737
to put a "Food Wars" twist

00:14:31.737 --> 00:14:33.172
on a Jack's godfather highball.

00:14:33.172 --> 00:14:34.073
Cocktail Time.

00:14:35.608 --> 00:14:36.242
Slight hiccup.

00:14:36.508 --> 00:14:37.443
Don't have a bottle opener.

00:14:39.578 --> 00:14:40.646
This is either going to work

00:14:40.646 --> 00:14:43.015
or I'm going to break my keys
and be locked out of my house.

00:14:48.487 --> 00:14:49.622
Improvisation.

00:14:50.189 --> 00:14:50.890
Slash.

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:51.657
Alcoholism.

00:14:51.991 --> 00:14:53.659
Ooh, it does smell quite smoky.

00:14:53.859 --> 00:14:56.362
Harry was kind enough to send me this,

00:14:56.362 --> 00:14:57.496
so now I have one as well.

00:14:57.663 --> 00:15:00.566
It just says, "Pour ingredients
into an ice-filled glass."

00:15:00.566 --> 00:15:03.769
Formally apologize to
any actual bartenders

00:15:03.769 --> 00:15:07.172
who are watching this while
I butcher your profession.

00:15:07.172 --> 00:15:10.376
30 milliliters of
Tennessee whiskey we have,

00:15:10.376 --> 00:15:12.211
and then 20 milliliters of Disaronno.

00:15:13.379 --> 00:15:14.813
A delightful smoky Coke.

00:15:17.316 --> 00:15:18.651
Next we mix together.

00:15:20.719 --> 00:15:21.987
And there you have it. Thanks to Coke,

00:15:21.987 --> 00:15:24.857
we've put our own spin on a
Jack's godfather highball.

00:15:24.857 --> 00:15:25.691
Cheers.

00:15:27.326 --> 00:15:28.661
Ooh. That's delicious.

00:15:28.894 --> 00:15:32.431
Um, yeah, I'm not going
to make that drink,

00:15:32.431 --> 00:15:33.499
'cause I don't have all that stuff.

00:15:33.499 --> 00:15:35.834
So I'm going to go ahead
and make a Joe highball.

00:15:36.001 --> 00:15:38.771
First, get yourself the
biggest glass available.

00:15:38.771 --> 00:15:40.506
Step two: no ice.

00:15:40.506 --> 00:15:41.440
Find yourself some whiskey.

00:15:51.483 --> 00:15:52.117
Cheers, my man.

00:15:56.722 --> 00:15:57.823
Oh, man.

00:15:58.924 --> 00:15:59.858
What is in this?

00:15:59.858 --> 00:16:01.760
If I was to do it again,
I'd use less of this.

00:16:03.429 --> 00:16:04.430
It's iced tea, guys.

00:16:05.564 --> 00:16:06.765
I'm not gonna f---ing drink whiskey

00:16:06.765 --> 00:16:07.733
this early in the morning.

00:16:09.568 --> 00:16:10.369
You know what it tastes like?

00:16:10.636 --> 00:16:11.737
Flat Coke.

00:16:11.971 --> 00:16:13.038
Oh, man, I'm getting a headache though.

00:16:13.238 --> 00:16:16.108
Last but not least, in the
US, you have the option

00:16:16.108 --> 00:16:18.243
to order customized Coke bottles.

00:16:18.243 --> 00:16:19.878
Check out the one I made.

00:16:19.878 --> 00:16:21.714
Joe and Harry.

00:16:28.287 --> 00:16:30.122
Here's everything that's
in a 500-milliliter bottle

00:16:30.122 --> 00:16:32.124
of Coca-Cola in the UK.

00:16:32.124 --> 00:16:33.659
And here's everything in that same bottle

00:16:33.659 --> 00:16:35.094
of classic Coke in the US.

00:16:36.562 --> 00:16:37.663
That means that the UK's version

00:16:37.663 --> 00:16:39.732
actually has slightly more
calories in it than the US.

00:16:39.765 --> 00:16:41.033
Joe: And we have more sugar.

00:16:41.033 --> 00:16:43.502
And for some reason, our Coke
has a little bit of sodium,

00:16:43.502 --> 00:16:45.104
while the UK seems to have none.

00:16:45.237 --> 00:16:47.840
Obviously, the main thing to
look out for here is the sugar.

00:16:47.840 --> 00:16:50.109
500 milliliters in both the US and the UK

00:16:50.109 --> 00:16:52.344
contains over 100% of
your daily allowance.

00:16:52.344 --> 00:16:55.047
53 grams of sugar. [laughs]

00:16:55.047 --> 00:16:56.448
It does put it in perspective, doesn't it?

00:16:56.448 --> 00:16:57.883
You never see it laid out like that,

00:16:57.883 --> 00:16:59.318
but that is how much sugar is in Coke.

00:16:59.318 --> 00:17:00.953
And I drink a lot of Coke.

00:17:00.953 --> 00:17:01.420
That's concerning.

00:17:01.553 --> 00:17:03.789
It's also worth noting that both countries

00:17:03.789 --> 00:17:05.758
put the same amount of
caffeine in their Coke.

00:17:05.858 --> 00:17:07.626
For reference, the average
cup of filtered coffee

00:17:07.626 --> 00:17:09.628
contains about 96 milligrams of caffeine.

00:17:09.695 --> 00:17:11.964
So that's exactly double the
amount in this bottle of Coke.

00:17:12.031 --> 00:17:14.033
Interestingly, diet Coke is
actually more caffeinated

00:17:14.033 --> 00:17:14.900
than regular Coke.

00:17:14.933 --> 00:17:16.668
There's 63 milligrams in this bottle,

00:17:16.668 --> 00:17:17.936
which is a 30% increase.

00:17:18.070 --> 00:17:20.539
And it makes sense, 'cause
our Coke with coffee

00:17:20.539 --> 00:17:24.143
contains 69 milligrams of
caffeine per 12 fluid ounces.

00:17:24.143 --> 00:17:26.078
If you do the math to find
out the figure per ounce,

00:17:26.078 --> 00:17:27.679
it's double the caffeine
of a regular Coke.

00:17:27.679 --> 00:17:31.150
But the real caffeine king
is my boy Coke Energy.

00:17:33.419 --> 00:17:34.353
Mm.

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:37.823
Whether you get the classic or the cherry,

00:17:37.823 --> 00:17:41.727
the 12-ounce can contains
114 milligrams of caffeine,

00:17:41.727 --> 00:17:43.729
which is triple the caffeine content

00:17:43.729 --> 00:17:45.998
of a regular Coke per ounce.

00:17:45.998 --> 00:17:48.300
Yo, don't I know it.

00:17:48.300 --> 00:17:49.535
I'm going to chug as much of this as I can

00:17:49.535 --> 00:17:51.270
without throwing up and
then see what we can do.

00:17:53.505 --> 00:17:56.075
[burps loudly]

00:17:56.075 --> 00:17:57.076
God, that's so gross.

00:17:57.076 --> 00:17:59.211
The max I got to there was 90 decibels,

00:17:59.211 --> 00:18:00.712
which, according to this thing I found,

00:18:00.712 --> 00:18:03.715
is about as loud as a leaf
blower, which is pretty good.

